  "limitations": [
    "No existing Marketing Agents SQLite database or volume was found during bounded local inventory. The user authorized a fresh seeded primary in that case. No records were migrated and no existing SQLite files, unrelated volumes or checkpoint refs are removed.",
    "PostgreSQL 17 Compose and the installed supported native PostgreSQL version are separate local qualifications. Native backups require matching major versions. This does not qualify production upgrades, hosted PostgreSQL, cross-major recovery, replication, availability or measured RPO/RTO.",
    "Single-operator local identity and deterministic mocks remain unchanged. No live provider delivery, production authentication, secure erasure, application database encryption or universal exactly-once external effects are claimed.",
    "Acquisition can contact registries; required runtime suites run under existing offline/network controls. The web ingress bridge retains its disclosed outbound route. This is not a fresh AC-15 four-suite kernel-isolation qualification.",
    "The original 20-gate quality inventory stays unchanged. Acceptance adds PostgreSQL recovery without removing legacy SQLite recovery, and clean-state adds explicit PostgreSQL execution without relaxing its 1620-second execution or 120-second cleanup budgets.",
    "Historical evidence remains bound to its original SQLite/default source. Full observed results are reported separately after freezing; focused diagnostics and optional skips do not qualify the candidate. Unsigned local attestations establish consistency, not independently authenticated execution.",
    "No publication or main merge is authorized by this manifest. Preserve all checkpoints; keep CI disabled. Store sanitized evidence outside Git and never publish a database/key backup bundle or credential-bearing output."
  ]
